  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1245 PM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nWarm and Dry Conditions: This persistence forecast will largely\nprevail through the end of the week however daily temps will \nclimb a few degrees each day. This is due to southerly low level\nwinds and an increase in 850mb temps (closer to 15-18C). NBM \ntemp spreads are small with highs in the middle to potentially \nupper 80s Wednesday through Sunday. These temps are roughly\n10-15 degrees above average for early October. Daily RH values \nin the 25-35% range will continue however winds still look to \nremain fairly low. Will need to monitor for any days/periods \nwhere winds can increase as this would increase the fire spread\nthreat. \n\nRain Chances?: There are a couple of systems that give us some\nhope for rainfall however both systems are not really in the\npicture until at least Sunday. This leads to high confidence in\ndry conditions for the remainder of the week and perhaps all\nweekend. There is currently energy in the western part of the Gulf\nof America that some ensemble model members want to develop \ninto a tropical system over the coming days. We will want to \ntrack that however current ensembles suggest this energy \nremaining east of our region if it does develop and move inland.\nThe other rain opportunity would be about 7-8 days from now as \nensembles suggest an upper trough moving into the northern US. \nConfidence in both these systems is low and the drought is \nlikely to persist and worsen this week due to the lack of \nrainfall.",
